+## Proposed existing scalar field metadata editing — [PR #27](https://github.com/sveltery/cms/pull/27)
+
+Immutable source is EmDash 1.1.0 `913cb1bb9b7f08c3ff0d258b4420e53835b6a58e`; base is CMS main `8c773d815bb54499d5d3eeca4f92b28d7b42ac22`. The [feature/source record](../../docs/field-edit.md) and [assertion ledger](../../docs/field-edit-ports.json) extend the landed label-only surface without changing historical FL-01–FL-03 or its one-expression run evidence. Optional labels retain exact nonempty/untrimmed/unbounded values. Supplied order/string-default/length-validation columns alone change; objects replace, null clears SQL NULL, and {} remains distinct. No field CAS, collection timestamp/version touch, SQL default/index change or content rewrite occurs.
+
+| Record | Observable pinned upstream / local behavior | Rationale and evidence status |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| FE-01: strict string/text edit slice | Upstream updateField accepts wider properties, unknown/null defaults and strips unknown request keys. Local accepts only optional label/order/string default/nullable length-validation and rejects unsupported keys/types, including null default. SQL NULL validation projects as upstream undefined versus retained local null. | Extend faithful supplied-key metadata semantics within the existing scalar product scope. String-only/default-null exclusions and nullable projection are explicit bounds/differences; broader fields remain incomplete. Source and local storage tests are separate from proposed deviation acceptance. |
+| FE-02: native modes, receipts and refresh | Upstream JSON PUT/React callbacks return a full field. Local flat Kit form uses explicit keep/set/validation-clear modes, validated stripped instance identity, native issues and bounded collection/field receipt, followed by query refreshes. | Preserve omission/null/object/empty-string semantics through native HTML and independent Kit instances. Transport and UI tests are supplemental; no REST/React/MCP-envelope credit. |
+| FE-03: inherited authorization/atomic subsystem limits | Upstream schema routes inspect configuration before permissions and registry updates reselect within withTransaction, notify type generation and invalidate media/cache state; D1 can fall back to separate statements. Local retains permission-before-storage/configuration, default-disabled gate, adapter-proven atomic UPDATE RETURNING receipt and schema/manifest refreshes; media/type-generation subsystems are absent. | Existing FL-02/FL-03, C-07/SA-03 policy continues unchanged. No field CAS, collection timestamp/schema-version touch, physical DDL or content rewrite is added. Selected field semantics do not grant subsystem/deployed-runtime parity. |
+
+
+The pinned complete-source reference passed 16 Node/local D1 tests (four selected runtime cases, twelve original supplements); the paired local suite passed eight (four selected, four supplements), including all 12 string/text optional/required initial-default layouts per runtime. Registry.test.ts:668 retains two of three expressions, omitting widget; MCP schema.test.ts:1003 retains both exact direct-registry concurrent label/order expressions with adapted setup. Of these four expressions, the prior label-only expression is already covered; three unique expressions are newly covered. One complete selected declaration with adapted setup and one partial declaration are credited, not MCP transport or the whole schema family. MCP schema.test.ts:982 only inspires supplemental before/after validation observations, earning zero source assertions/declarations.
+
+Cleared validation SQL NULL maps upstream undefined versus retained local null (SA-02). SF-02 existing physical divergence, SF-03 required-empty content behavior, C-07/SA-03 atomicity and inherited unenforced unique metadata/issue #20 remain unchanged. No production access/activation, deployment, publishing, permanent deletion or existing-table reconstruction is included. Specific acceptance of intentional differences is not recorded. Full bootstrap, secured default/Node browsers, exact-head independent/configured review and final CI remain required; merge and post-merge CI must be recorded separately.
